Z||000000||Neverfinished||02-09-2001||01:47 AM||||what are these "spark plugs" I keep hearing about???<BR>Do they attch to your headights or something?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jake||02-09-2001||02:15 AM||||actually they don't connect to your headlights like most people think. What they really do is fit in behind your dash. That's where they play there part. When you turn your headlight switch on they spark a gas line which creates a pilot light behind your dash lights so you can see your gauges at night<P>P.S. don't forget to check your horn oil, bumper fluid and tail-pipe bearings on a regular basis.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Neverfinished||02-09-2001||02:40 AM||||I can't believe how much they are charging for high performance air for my tires and water for my engine. Isn't the spark plug that thing that glows in the headlight thingy???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||02-09-2001||03:00 AM||||Don't forget to check the blinker fluid and the johnson rods!  ||||reg||1
